 "result_text": "I fixed it in `get_keys` in `sshtunnel.py`. When `host_pkey_directories` is `None` (the default), it now searches `DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY` (`~/.ssh`). Before, a `None` value skipped the key search entirely, so the `or [DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY]` fallback never ran. An explicit list is still searched as given. An explicit empty list now searches nothing; before, it fell back to `~/.ssh`.\n\nThe test suite gives 48 passed and 2 failed: `test_connect_via_proxy` (a `FileNotFoundError`) and `test_read_ssh_config` (an `AttributeError`). I didn't run the suite before the change or look into either failure. Neither test covers the `get_keys` path I changed, so I haven't confirmed they're unrelated. I didn't add a test for the fix, as instructed, and I haven't committed anything.",
